{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"length","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"People run language models on their own computers because the cloud is convenient, but it is not always the best fit. For many users, the main reason is privacy. Prompts, documents, code, medical notes, legal drafts, and personal conversations can reveal sensitive information. Keeping a model local means that data does not have to leave the machine, and the user is not fully dependent on a provider’s logging, retention, or access policies.\n\nCost is another factor. Cloud APIs are easy to start with, but usage can grow quickly and become expensive, especially for heavy or repeated workloads. A local setup can be paid for once through hardware and then used repeatedly, which may be cheaper over","reasoning_content":"The user wants a short essay in English about why people run language models on their own computers instead of in the cloud. Need produce final answer only. Need ensure essay is short, coherent, maybe 4-6 paragraphs or one cohesive short essay. Need discuss privacy, cost, control, latency, offline/reliability, customization, data sovereignty, security, independence from providers, experimentation. Avoid overclaiming. Mention tradeoffs briefly. Need answer in English. No need for citations. Need be careful not to include hidden thinking. Final should be just essay.\n\nNeed craft concise essay. Maybe title optional. Short essay ~250-350 words. Ensure directly addresses why. Let's draft.\n\nPotential structure:\n- Intro: cloud convenient but not always best.\n- Privacy/data control: prompts/documents stay local; sensitive medical/legal/personal data; no third-party logs.\n- Cost/predictability: pay-as-you-go can be expensive at scale; local hardware amortizes; no per-token fees.\n- Latency/offline: local inference faster/no network dependency; works without internet; lower latency for interactive use.\n- Control/customization: fine-tune, quantize, choose models, run open-source, avoid vendor lock-in.\n- Security/trust: fewer external dependencies, auditability, compliance.\n- Tradeoffs: hardware cost, maintenance, less scalability; cloud still better for many.\n- Conclusion: local runs for autonomy/privacy/control, not because cloud is bad.\n\nNeed maybe mention own computers can mean laptops/desktops/servers. Keep short. Ensure no markdown excessive? Fine.\n\nNeed final only."}}],"created":1795504350,"model":"/models/unsloth/Inkling-2-Mini-GGUF/Inkling-2-Mini-UD-Q3_K_XL.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b12651-d426a3774","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":512,"prompt_tokens":37,"total_tokens":549,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-xbfhv57Xk2xpoBIdJXWcNPcoFKsfrN4n","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":37,"prompt_ms":188.059,"prompt_per_token_ms":5.0826756756756755,"prompt_per_second":196.74676564269723,"predicted_n":512,"predicted_ms":10326.633,"predicted_per_token_ms":20.208675146771036,"predicted_per_second":49.48369909146573,"draft_n":770,"draft_n_accepted":253}}
